speechtext:
I move that clause 15 be struck out and that the following be substituted therefor:
15. The works and undertakings of the following companies are hereby declared to be works for the general advantage of Canada viz.:
Canadian Northern Manitoba Railway Company ;
Irondale, Bancroft and Ottawa Railway Company ;
Marmora Railway and Mining Company;
Halifax and Southwestern Railway Company ;
Quebec and Lake St. John Railway Company.
2.	The works and undertakings of the Canadian Northern Western Railway Company are hereby declared to be works for the general advantage of Canada.
3.	The works and undertakings of the Canadian Northern Saskatchewan Railway Company are hereby declared to be works for the general advantage of Canada.
4.	The works and undertakings of the Canadian Northern Pacific Railway Company are hereby declared to be works for the general advantage of Canada.
5.	Subsections 2, 3 and 4 shall respectively come into force on a day or days to be fixed in each case by proclamation of the Governor in Council published in the Canada Gazette, but such proclamation shall not in any case be made until after the Governor in Council shall have declared in each such case by Order in Council that the railway and undertaking of such company has been constructed and is open for operation.
